# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXUS DIGITAL — environment notes
#
# This app is a STATIC Vite build deployed to Netlify. It has no backend and no
# serverless functions: the browser talks directly to the Firebase Realtime
# Database. Nothing below is required at build time, and there are no secrets
# to configure on Netlify — do NOT put credentials in this file.
#
# Copy to `.env` only for local development if you need to override defaults.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Local dev only. Netlify sets its own PORT and prefers the published static
# files; `server.ts` is never run in production.
# PORT=3000

# Local dev convenience: disables Vite HMR + file watching.
# DISABLE_HMR=false

# ───────────────────────────── Firebase (browser) ────────────────────────────
# The Firebase web config is intentionally hard-coded in index.html and
# admin/index.html under `const firebaseConfig = { ... }`. A Firebase *web*
# API key is a public project identifier, not a secret — it is meant to be
# visible in the client. Security is enforced by Firebase Security Rules and by
# restricting the key in Google Cloud Console (HTTP referrers + API list).
#
# To point the site at a different Firebase project, edit `firebaseConfig` in
# BOTH files, then lock the key down:
#   https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials  → restrict the key
#   Realtime Database → Rules                        → deny-by-default
#
# Because writes happen from the browser, database rules — not this file — are
# the real access control. At minimum, prevent clients from:
#   - writing to settings/* except via the admin console
#   - crediting customers/*/walletCoins directly
#   - reading other customers' records
#
# Minimum viable rule set (adapt before going live with real money):
#
# {
#   "rules": {
#     "products":      { ".read": true,  ".write": "auth != null" },
#     "reviews":       { ".read": true,  ".write": true },
#     "settings":      { ".read": true,  ".write": "auth != null" },
#     "dollarRequests":{ ".read": "auth != null", ".write": true },
#     "addFunds":      { ".read": "auth != null", ".write": true },
#     "deposits":      { ".read": "auth != null", ".write": true },
#     "cashouts":      { ".read": "auth != null", ".write": true },
#     "orders":        { ".read": "auth != null", ".write": true },
#     "transactions":  { ".read": "auth != null", ".write": "auth != null" },
#     "customers":     { "$uid": { ".read": true, ".write": true } }
#   }
# }
#
# The rules above keep the CURRENT feature set working. They are permissive by
# design because wallet debits/credits are performed by the client. Before
# handling real money, move balance mutation behind a trusted server
# (Netlify Function or Firebase Cloud Function) and tighten accordingly.
